WEBVTT

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:41.930
Chief, please read this.
after closing.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.620
Dear Chief,

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.290
Please look after
Taro and Hanako.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.030
From Kasumi

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.960
Kasumi ran off
with a customer?

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.290
W-What'll we do?

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.420
Papa!

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:46.450
M-Manager!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.910
Godai?

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.170
Who are these kids?

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.760
well

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:01.720
Here.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.290
Thank you.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.970
What a healthy child.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.510
Who's that baby?

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.800
Is she yours?

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.940
A love-child.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.170
So you've both
been hiding them?

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.160
The things people do
when they're desperate.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.510
Godai's a man, after all

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.670
Y-Yusaku!

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.000
Cut it out!!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.760
Sorry. It's those
people's fault

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:39.700
It's okay.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.700
A hostess ran off?!

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:52.700
Yeah.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.700
So it was decided that
I take them overnight.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.300
Poor things. They
don't know anything.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.320
What're you gonna do

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.730
if the mother
doesn't come back?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.130
I'll find her.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.580
Where?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.420
I don't know!

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.170
How haphazard.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:18.310
In the worst-case scenario,
this man will be your papa.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.660
Papa! Papa!

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.570
What are you going to do
with them tomorrow?

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:33.250
Why don't you keep them here
until you find their mother?

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.700
Is that okay?

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.760
Do you want to stay here?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.820
He's got the manager duped.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.590
Quite a little scamp, this kid.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.530
Stop seeing things
in such a twisted way!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.450
Geez! How could she abandon
such adorable kids!

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.180
It's okay.
Be a good girl

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.080
What's with the noise?!

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.210
Can't help it!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.130
It's okay.
You're a good girl

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.610
Godai?

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.260
Manager.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.160
Is she colicky?

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.610
I'm sorry.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.610
It's not easy, is it?

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.710
Let me hold her awhile.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:13.900
I can't impose.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.030
It's okay.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.460
She's asleep already.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.160
She was just
crying so hard.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.160
I guess she feels
more comforted

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.010
in a woman's arms.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:42.340
You!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.200
Godai.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.300
Kyoko.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.440
It's leaking.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.390
Her diaper's leaking.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:42.510
I know you have
a lot to do.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.720
Thanks for your help.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.240
Taro, be sure to listen
to everybody.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:52.640
Don't worry
about the baby.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.510
We've got experience.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.190
Well, I'm off.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:03.120
Chief, bye!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.320
Well, well

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:11.090
Godai sure has a knack

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:14.030
of finding new things
to worry about.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.680
But it's very much like him.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.610
I guess.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.530
Right?

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.180
Hello!

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.260
Hi Godai. You're early.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.920
Any word from Kasumi?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.230
Nothing.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.930
Hey, I heard Kasumi ran away.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:47.990
I figured she would.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.160
You "figured she would"?

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.100
She's infamous in
the hostess circle.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.510
Every time she starts
at a new place,

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.250
she runs off
with a customer.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:03.890
So this isn't the first time
she's dumped her kids?

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.640
That's unforgivable!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.040
It may be futile, but.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.050
You want to go to
Kasumi's apartment?

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:16.560
It's here.
You can go tomorrow.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.140
Yes.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:24.140
How unusual of you
to come home, Shun.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:27.980
Why so glum? You don't
get here very often.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:31.010
You picked a good day,
since your father's office is closed

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.800
in observance of its
anniversary of establishment.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.590
That's why I'm here.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.330
Father, Mother.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.230
What's with the formality?

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.600
There's someone I'd
like you to meet.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.830
Someone you'd
like us to meet?

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.020
What kind of person is this?

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:56.430
The one I'd like to.

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:57.920
marry.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.430
Asuna Kujo, right?

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.640
We met her the other day.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.120
It's another woman!

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:10.220
Uncle set me up
against my will!

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.440
Too bad. She seems like
a great young woman.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.250
I'm serious!

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.960
I don't care what anyone says.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.020
Before you object, I want you
to meet her in person and-

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.630
When?

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.000
When shall we meet her?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.250
I-Is that.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.980
okay...with you?

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.580
Why not?!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.080
I wonder what this woman is like?!

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.750
I can't wait to meet her!

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:43.990
This is great!

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:50.520
That's it?! I should have
told them earlier.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.420
Chigusa residence.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.560
Mitaka?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.270
Hello, Mrs. Chigusa.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.430
I called because.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:14.120
You want us to have dinner
with your parents?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.120
Sure. We'd love to.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.390
Then I will call Kyoko.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:23.640
Please! Let me call Kyoko.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.120
You know, if we bring up
the talk of marriage,

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.790
she'd get all tensed up.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.640
Don't you worry. I'll get her
there somehow.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.240
Sure. Leave it to me.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:39.430
Good-bye, then.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:43.380
This is it!

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.580
Now that I've managed
to come this far...

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:50.110
There's no turning
back now, Kyoko.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:52.680
Full speed ahead!

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.010
As fast as you can go.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.920
Sleeping, so carefree.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:08.710
Looks like a mother
and her kids.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:12.470
They have no idea what
position they're in.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:16.030
Neither does Yusaku.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:41.560
Manager, I'm going to
Kasumi"s apartment today.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.510
If she's at her apartment,

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.560
then she wouldn't need
to ask you to take her kids.

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.670
I know...

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.210
I heard Kasumi ran off.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:52.710
I figured she would.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.180
She's infamous in
the hostess circle.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.510
Evey time she starts
at a new place,

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.680
she runs off
with a customer.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:07.970
When I find her,

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.290
I'm going to give her
a piece of my mind.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.720
Moonlight Villa
Here it is.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:37.960
Kasumi!

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.460
Kasumi!

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.020
Kasumi?!
Are you in there?!

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.040
She's not here.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.780
What're you think you're doing,
you creep!

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:10.120
Kasumi!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.250
Chief?

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:14.490
What are you doing here?

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.520
C-Could you turn off
the shower?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.660
Sorry, Chief.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.670
You scared me.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.530
You're the one
who scared me.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.640
I thought you ran off
with a man?!

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:51.230
Here. Have a drink, Chief.

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:54.760
Cheers!

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:00.470
Nothing like a cold beer
after a bath!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.350
Shall we get going, Kasumi?

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:04.210
Where?

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:05.750
To my apartment

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.440
Your children are
waiting for you.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.370
W-What are you doing?

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.510
Are you listening to me?

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:22.370
Take some change of
clothes for them.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.020
Clothes?

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.300
Why?

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.210
I have to go on
a Journey now.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.980
What are you thinking?

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:36.720
One week. Please give me
one week, Chief.

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.800
No way. And you call
yourself a mother?!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:48.310
Then are you willing
to marry me, Chief?

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.590
Why me?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.890
You won't, would you?!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:59.920
What's the matter, Hanako?

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:02.530
You got milk.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:04.510
She's not wet

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.610
What'll we do?
She won't stop crying.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:10.430
She just started.

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:11.980
What's wrong?

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.720
Take it easy, Manager.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:20.830
Snow man, snow man, ducky.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:25.290
I'm looking for a man
who'll be my kids' Daddy.

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:27.680
The man I found this time
needs a little more push.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.690
While I travel
with him one week.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.060
What your kids need now
is their mother!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:36.160
My kids understand.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:38.100
No, they don't.

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:44.140
Wait a second.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.900
It's my pager.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:16:59.960
Hello? Mama?

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:05.300
Taro? What's the matter?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:11.250
Hanako won't stop crying?
Then do this.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.120
She said to hold
her up straight

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:17.520
and tap her back.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.150
Hold her up straight?
Like this?

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.850
I guess.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:28.450
You're doing okay,
aren't you?

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.490
I'll come and get you
In one week.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.180
We'll be okay.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.190
Taro, may I?

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:37.960
Hello?
Is this the mother?

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:42.430
You're the manager of
Chief's apartment building?

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:45.960
Thank you so much for
taking care of my kids.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.840
I'll put him on.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:54.410
Godai? What's happening?

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:57.550
I'm going to bring
the mother over now-

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.380
Hey!

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.980
Godai? What's going on?
Godai?

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:08.490
Hold it!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.370
Kasumi!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.790
Kasumi! Wait!

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:41.220
Chief! Please lock up!

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.390
Kasumi!

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:47.310
I'll be back in one week!
Please take care of my kids!

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.900
Kasumi! Wait!!

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:57.700
Kasumi.

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:13.270
And?

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.920
She got away.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.680
So what now?

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.190
This puts a damper on things.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.930
We can't party like
we usually do.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:27.190
What are you so
worried about?!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:28.880
Let's party!

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:33.380
You're a spunky kid.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.060
We have no choice.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.770
Since Taro insists.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.390
Let's party hearty!

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:51.270
Let's!

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.000
Thank you for
looking after Hanako.

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:09.610
Go and relax.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:11.680
Bye!

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:15.150
See you!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:22.110
Godai's not going
to the cabaret?

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.300
He has a night off.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:25.860
Shucks.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:26.880
Why?

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:37.700
Otonashi speak-.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.550
Oh, hi Mom.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:43.390
I'm calling about
this Saturday.

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:46.940
Dad's birthday?
Dinner at a hotel?

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:49.720
You better make your dad
happy once in a while.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.650
- All right?
- Well, sure.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:56.540
Three o'clock, then.
Don't forget, Kyoko.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.700
Dad's birthday's
in September.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.640
Mitaka?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:18.290
She said she'll come?

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.400
She was very happy.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:25.420
Yes. Saturday..at 3:00. Yes.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:29.370
My parents and I are looking
forward to seeing you.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.250
Saturday. Three o'clock.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.940
This is great, McEnroe!

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:00.450
Hey, not too rough.
You're going to fall off.

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:09.400
Nothing gets
this child down.

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:23.170
Taro, don't you
feel lonely?

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:24.970
Not a bit.

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:30.030
Let's hope your mom
comes back soon.

00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:32.450
She made a promise
on a star.

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:35.060
- Star?
- Uh-huh.

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:51.970
Listen, Taro.
I promise on that star

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:55.790
that I'll come back
In one week.

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:58.320
Sounds like Kasumi.

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:02.150
So you believe..

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:04.490
in your Mama.

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:09.370
She wouldn't lie to a star.

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:14.840
Of course she'll be back.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:21.340
It's a shooting star!

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.580
What are you doing?

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:30.740
Yusaku?

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:36.450
What was that?

00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:39.590
A UFO?

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:51.420
What? Kyoko and Mitaka?

00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:53.540
Their parents are
meeting each other.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:55.780
Then they're off to a hotel
with a view of the harbor.

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:58.200
You just know something's
going to happen.

00:23:58.360 --> 00:23:59.580
N-No!

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:01.050
Kyoko!

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:04.460
Next: "Off to the Yokohama Border!
Kyoko's Doing a Runner"

00:24:04.530 --> 00:24:06.500
woman Can be swayed
by the right mood.
